IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `lga-concession`

-- Local Government Act 1993 (NSW), ss 575-584, with the Local Government (General) Regulation 2021, cll 134-136 --
-- the pensioner rates concession, from the seat of the eligible pensioner.
--
-- SEAT: the eligible pensioner liable (solely or jointly) for council rates and charges on the dwelling they live in.
-- "Am I an eligible pensioner for this dwelling? How much are my rates and charges reduced this year, alone or with a
-- co-owner? What if I became a pensioner mid-year? When does my concession stop, and is anything credited? Can the
-- council later recover what it wrote off?" Every question is phrased as that person would ask it, on facts that
-- person could state. The rules are in lga-concession.l4; this module builds the core's records from plain answers
-- and restates no rule. The council is a public body and has no seat.
--
-- The 27 answers of the main question are asked in the same order wherever they appear, so the form can ask them
-- once: nine about Commonwealth payments and cards, two about the dwelling, five about who else is liable, five
-- amounts, three dates, three about council relief.
--
-- EDITION: act-1993-030 (2025-01-01) and sl-2021-0460 (2024-09-02), Open Australian Legal Corpus as at 10 March 2025:
-- NOT THE CURRENT OFFICIAL TEXT AND MAY BE OUT OF DATE. The $250 and $87.50 caps are the deposited text's.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Pensioner rates concession -- the pensioner's questions`

-- Builders: plain answers into the core's records.

GIVEN `ssa` IS A BOOLEAN, `vea service` IS A BOOLEAN, `pcc` IS A BOOLEAN, `war widow` IS A BOOLEAN, `mother` IS A BOOLEAN, `mrca 234` IS A BOOLEAN, `means test` IS A BOOLEAN, `vea rate` IS A BOOLEAN, `srdp` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Commonwealth payments and card`
`my Commonwealth payments and card from` `ssa` `vea service` `pcc` `war widow` `mother` `mrca 234` `means test` `vea rate` `srdp` MEANS
    `Commonwealth payments and card` WITH
        `receives a pension, benefit or allowance under Chapter 2 of the Social Security Act 1991` IS `ssa`
        `receives a service pension under Part III of the Veterans' Entitlements Act 1986`        IS `vea service`
        `is entitled to a pensioner concession card`                                              IS `pcc`
        `receives a DVA pension as a war widow or war widower`                                    IS `war widow`
        `receives a DVA pension as the unmarried or widowed mother of a deceased unmarried member of the Defence or Peacekeeping Forces` IS `mother`
        `has received the MRCA s 234(1)(b) lump sum or receives the weekly amount`                IS `mrca 234`
        `has income and assets that would not prevent the grant of a pensioner concession card`   IS `means test`
        `receives the VEA s 22(4) extreme disablement rate or the s 24 special rate`              IS `vea rate`
        `receives, or has at some time been eligible for, the MRCA Special Rate Disability Pension` IS `srdp`

GIVEN `dwelling` IS A BOOLEAN, `home` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Occupation of the land`
`my occupation from` `dwelling` `home` MEANS
    `Occupation of the land` WITH
        `a dwelling is situated on the land`                          IS `dwelling`
        `occupies that dwelling as sole or principal place of living` IS `home`

-- The other persons liable, by which limb of "jointly eligible occupier" (if any) each meets. Each record carries only
-- what the definition reads; the last is a person who meets no limb, or does not live with the pensioner.
`a spouse or de facto partner living with me` MEANS
    `Other person liable` WITH
        `is the spouse or de facto partner of the eligible pensioner` IS TRUE
        `is another eligible pensioner` IS FALSE
        `is the spouse or de facto partner of another eligible pensioner who has the same sole or principal place of dwelling` IS FALSE
        `has the same sole or principal place of living as the eligible pensioner` IS TRUE

`another eligible pensioner living with me` MEANS
    `Other person liable` WITH
        `is the spouse or de facto partner of the eligible pensioner` IS FALSE
        `is another eligible pensioner` IS TRUE
        `is the spouse or de facto partner of another eligible pensioner who has the same sole or principal place of dwelling` IS FALSE
        `has the same sole or principal place of living as the eligible pensioner` IS TRUE

`the spouse or de facto partner of another eligible pensioner, living with me` MEANS
    `Other person liable` WITH
        `is the spouse or de facto partner of the eligible pensioner` IS FALSE
        `is another eligible pensioner` IS FALSE
        `is the spouse or de facto partner of another eligible pensioner who has the same sole or principal place of dwelling` IS TRUE
        `has the same sole or principal place of living as the eligible pensioner` IS TRUE

`a person liable who is none of these` MEANS
    `Other person liable` WITH
        `is the spouse or de facto partner of the eligible pensioner` IS FALSE
        `is another eligible pensioner` IS FALSE
        `is the spouse or de facto partner of another eligible pensioner who has the same sole or principal place of dwelling` IS FALSE
        `has the same sole or principal place of living as the eligible pensioner` IS FALSE

GIVEN `n spouse` IS A NUMBER, `n pensioners` IS A NUMBER, `n their partners` IS A NUMBER, `n others` IS A NUMBER, `the part` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Liability for the rates`
`my liability from` `n spouse` `n pensioners` `n their partners` `n others` `the part` MEANS
    `Liability for the rates` WITH
        `the other persons liable` IS concat (LIST (replicate `n spouse` `a spouse or de facto partner living with me`), (replicate `n pensioners` `another eligible pensioner living with me`), (replicate `n their partners` `the spouse or de facto partner of another eligible pensioner, living with me`), (replicate `n others` `a person liable who is none of these`))
        `the part for which the applicant and any jointly eligible occupier are liable, as between all persons liable` IS `the part`

GIVEN `ordinary` IS A NUMBER, `waste` IS A NUMBER, `water` IS A NUMBER, `sewerage` IS A NUMBER, `other` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Rates and charges levied for the year`
`my rates from` `ordinary` `waste` `water` `sewerage` `other` MEANS
    `Rates and charges levied for the year` WITH
        `ordinary rates`                        IS `ordinary`
        `domestic waste management charges`     IS `waste`
        `water supply special rates or charges` IS `water`
        `sewerage special rates or charges`     IS `sewerage`
        `other rates or charges`                IS `other`

GIVEN `varied` IS A BOOLEAN, `hardship` IS A BOOLEAN, `waiver` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Council relief and regulations`
`the relief from` `varied` `hardship` `waiver` MEANS
    `Council relief and regulations` WITH
        `a regulation under s 580 varies the amounts`       IS `varied`
        `a council hardship order under s 577 applies`      IS `hardship`
        `a council waiver or reduction under s 582 applies` IS `waiver`

§§ `Am I an eligible pensioner?`

@export Which class of pensioner prescribed by the NSW Local Government (General) Regulation 2021, cl 134, am I in, for the council rates concession?
GIVEN `I receive a pension, benefit or allowance under Chapter 2 of the Social Security Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you receive a Centrelink payment under Chapter 2 of the Social Security Act 1991 (Cth), such as the age pension, disability support pension, carer payment, parenting payment, JobSeeker payment or youth allowance
      `I receive a service pension under Part III of the Veterans' Entitlements Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you receive a DVA service pension (age or invalidity service pension) under Part III of the Veterans' Entitlements Act 1986 (Cth)
      `I am entitled to a pensioner concession card` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are entitled to a Commonwealth pensioner concession card, issued by Centrelink or DVA (a health care card or Commonwealth seniors health card is a different card: answer no)
      `I receive a DVA pension as a war widow or war widower` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you receive a pension from the Department of Veterans' Affairs as a war widow or war widower within the meaning of the Veterans' Entitlements Act 1986
      `I receive a DVA pension as the unmarried or widowed mother of a deceased unmarried member of the Defence or Peacekeeping Forces` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you receive a DVA pension as the unmarried mother, or the widowed mother, of a deceased unmarried member of the Australian Defence or Peacekeeping Forces
      `I have received the MRCA s 234(1)(b) lump sum or receive the weekly amount` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, as the wholly dependent partner of a deceased member, you have received the lump sum or receive the weekly amount mentioned in s 234(1)(b) of the Military Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2004 (Cth)
      `my income and assets would not stop me being granted a pensioner concession card` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your income and assets are within the limits for a pensioner concession card, assuming you were otherwise eligible for one (asked for war widows, mothers and MRCA partners only)
      `I receive the VEA extreme disablement rate or special rate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you receive a DVA disability pension at the extreme disablement adjustment rate (s 22(4)) or the special rate (s 24, often called TPI) of the Veterans' Entitlements Act 1986
      `I receive, or have at some time been eligible for, the MRCA Special Rate Disability Pension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you receive the Special Rate Disability Pension under the Military Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2004, or have been eligible for it at any time in your life
GIVETH A `Prescribed class`
DECIDE `Which class prescribed by cl 134 am I in` IS
    `the cl 134 class of` (`my Commonwealth payments and card from` `I receive a pension, benefit or allowance under Chapter 2 of the Social Security Act` `I receive a service pension under Part III of the Veterans' Entitlements Act` `I am entitled to a pensioner concession card` `I receive a DVA pension as a war widow or war widower` `I receive a DVA pension as the unmarried or widowed mother of a deceased unmarried member of the Defence or Peacekeeping Forces` `I have received the MRCA s 234(1)(b) lump sum or receive the weekly amount` `my income and assets would not stop me being granted a pensioner concession card` `I receive the VEA extreme disablement rate or special rate` `I receive, or have at some time been eligible for, the MRCA Special Rate Disability Pension`)

@export Am I an "eligible pensioner" for the council rates and charges on this land, under the NSW Local Government Act 1993 Dictionary and Regulation cl 134?
GIVEN `I receive a pension, benefit or allowance under Chapter 2 of the Social Security Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you receive a Centrelink payment under Chapter 2 of the Social Security Act 1991 (Cth), such as the age pension, disability support pension, carer payment, parenting payment, JobSeeker payment or youth allowance
      `I receive a service pension under Part III of the Veterans' Entitlements Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you receive a DVA service pension (age or invalidity service pension) under Part III of the Veterans' Entitlements Act 1986 (Cth)
      `I am entitled to a pensioner concession card` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are entitled to a Commonwealth pensioner concession card, issued by Centrelink or DVA (a health care card or Commonwealth seniors health card is a different card: answer no)
      `I receive a DVA pension as a war widow or war widower` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you receive a pension from the Department of Veterans' Affairs as a war widow or war widower within the meaning of the Veterans' Entitlements Act 1986
      `I receive a DVA pension as the unmarried or widowed mother of a deceased unmarried member of the Defence or Peacekeeping Forces` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you receive a DVA pension as the unmarried mother, or the widowed mother, of a deceased unmarried member of the Australian Defence or Peacekeeping Forces
      `I have received the MRCA s 234(1)(b) lump sum or receive the weekly amount` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, as the wholly dependent partner of a deceased member, you have received the lump sum or receive the weekly amount mentioned in s 234(1)(b) of the Military Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2004 (Cth)
      `my income and assets would not stop me being granted a pensioner concession card` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your income and assets are within the limits for a pensioner concession card, assuming you were otherwise eligible for one (asked for war widows, mothers and MRCA partners only)
      `I receive the VEA extreme disablement rate or special rate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you receive a DVA disability pension at the extreme disablement adjustment rate (s 22(4)) or the special rate (s 24, often called TPI) of the Veterans' Entitlements Act 1986
      `I receive, or have at some time been eligible for, the MRCA Special Rate Disability Pension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you receive the Special Rate Disability Pension under the Military Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2004, or have been eligible for it at any time in your life
      `there is a dwelling on the land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there is a dwelling on the land the rates are levied on: a building, or part of a building, used as a place to live (a house, a unit, a flat)
      `I live in that dwelling as my sole or principal place of living` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that dwelling is your only or main home
GIVETH AN `Eligible pensioner answer`
DECIDE `Am I an eligible pensioner for the rates on this land` IS
    `the eligible pensioner status of` (`my Commonwealth payments and card from` `I receive a pension, benefit or allowance under Chapter 2 of the Social Security Act` `I receive a service pension under Part III of the Veterans' Entitlements Act` `I am entitled to a pensioner concession card` `I receive a DVA pension as a war widow or war widower` `I receive a DVA pension as the unmarried or widowed mother of a deceased unmarried member of the Defence or Peacekeeping Forces` `I have received the MRCA s 234(1)(b) lump sum or receive the weekly amount` `my income and assets would not stop me being granted a pensioner concession card` `I receive the VEA extreme disablement rate or special rate` `I receive, or have at some time been eligible for, the MRCA Special Rate Disability Pension`) `on` (`my occupation from` `there is a dwelling on the land` `I live in that dwelling as my sole or principal place of living`)

@export Is this person, who is liable for the rates on my land with me, a "jointly eligible occupier" under the NSW Local Government Act 1993 Dictionary?
GIVEN `they are my spouse or de facto partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the other person is your husband, wife or de facto partner
      `they are an eligible pensioner too` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the other person is also an eligible pensioner: in one of the pensioner classes (the class question) and living in this dwelling as their only or main home
      `they are the spouse or de facto partner of another eligible pensioner who lives with them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the other person is the husband, wife or de facto partner of another eligible pensioner (not you), the two of them having the same only or main home
      `their only or main home is the same as mine` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the other person's only or main home is the same as yours
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this other person liable with me a jointly eligible occupier` IF
    `is a jointly eligible occupier` (`Other person liable` WITH
        `is the spouse or de facto partner of the eligible pensioner` IS `they are my spouse or de facto partner`
        `is another eligible pensioner` IS `they are an eligible pensioner too`
        `is the spouse or de facto partner of another eligible pensioner who has the same sole or principal place of dwelling` IS `they are the spouse or de facto partner of another eligible pensioner who lives with them`
        `has the same sole or principal place of living as the eligible pensioner` IS `their only or main home is the same as mine`)

§§ `How much are my rates and charges reduced?`

@export Which paragraph of s 575(2) of the NSW Local Government Act 1993 sets my pensioner reduction: one-half (alone, or only with jointly eligible occupiers), or my proportional share of one-half?
GIVEN `how many of the others liable are my spouse or de facto partner living with me` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of the other people liable for the rates on this land are your husband, wife or de facto partner whose only or main home is the same as yours (0 or 1; 0 if you are the only person liable)
      `how many of the others liable are other eligible pensioners living with me` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of the other people liable for the rates are themselves eligible pensioners living in this dwelling as their only or main home
      `how many of the others liable are the spouse or de facto partner of another eligible pensioner, living with me` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of the other people liable are the husband, wife or de facto partner of another eligible pensioner (not you), sharing that pensioner's home, which is also your only or main home
      `how many of the others liable are none of these` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of the other people liable for the rates are none of the above: for example a son or daughter who is not an eligible pensioner, a co-owner who lives elsewhere, or your spouse or partner if their main home is elsewhere
      `the part of the rates that I and those living with me are liable for` IS A NUMBER @desc As between all the people liable, the part of the rates that you and the people counted in the first three answers are liable for, as a fraction of the whole (for example 0.5 for half); used only if someone in the last group is liable with you
GIVETH A `s 575(2) paragraph`
DECIDE `Which paragraph of s 575(2) applies to me` IS
    `the s 575(2) paragraph for` (`my liability from` `how many of the others liable are my spouse or de facto partner living with me` `how many of the others liable are other eligible pensioners living with me` `how many of the others liable are the spouse or de facto partner of another eligible pensioner, living with me` `how many of the others liable are none of these` `the part of the rates that I and those living with me are liable for`)

-- Asked if you became a pensioner during the rating year.
@export If I became an eligible pensioner after my council rates were levied, how much of the year counts for the reduction (s 575(4) of the NSW Local Government Act 1993)?
GIVEN `the rating year` IS A NUMBER @desc The rating year the rates are for, named by the year it starts: 2025 for 1 July 2025 to 30 June 2026
      `the day my rates notice was served` IS A DATE @desc The day the council's rates and charges notice for that year was served on you (rates are levied by serving the notice)
      `the day I became an eligible pensioner` IS A DATE @desc The first day on which you met all the conditions of an eligible pensioner for this dwelling (any earlier day if you met them before the notice was served)
GIVETH A `s 575(4) position`
DECIDE `How much of the year counts if I became an eligible pensioner after my rates were levied` IS
    `the s 575(4) position for` `the rating year` `levied on` `the day my rates notice was served` `eligible from` `the day I became an eligible pensioner`

@export How much are my NSW council rates and charges reduced this year as an eligible pensioner (Local Government Act 1993 s 575 and Regulation cl 134), alone or with co-owners? The reduction is also the amount co-owners cannot ask me to contribute (s 575(5)).
GIVEN `I receive a pension, benefit or allowance under Chapter 2 of the Social Security Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you receive a Centrelink payment under Chapter 2 of the Social Security Act 1991 (Cth), such as the age pension, disability support pension, carer payment, parenting payment, JobSeeker payment or youth allowance
      `I receive a service pension under Part III of the Veterans' Entitlements Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you receive a DVA service pension (age or invalidity service pension) under Part III of the Veterans' Entitlements Act 1986 (Cth)
      `I am entitled to a pensioner concession card` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are entitled to a Commonwealth pensioner concession card, issued by Centrelink or DVA (a health care card or Commonwealth seniors health card is a different card: answer no)
      `I receive a DVA pension as a war widow or war widower` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you receive a pension from the Department of Veterans' Affairs as a war widow or war widower within the meaning of the Veterans' Entitlements Act 1986
      `I receive a DVA pension as the unmarried or widowed mother of a deceased unmarried member of the Defence or Peacekeeping Forces` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you receive a DVA pension as the unmarried mother, or the widowed mother, of a deceased unmarried member of the Australian Defence or Peacekeeping Forces
      `I have received the MRCA s 234(1)(b) lump sum or receive the weekly amount` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, as the wholly dependent partner of a deceased member, you have received the lump sum or receive the weekly amount mentioned in s 234(1)(b) of the Military Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2004 (Cth)
      `my income and assets would not stop me being granted a pensioner concession card` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your income and assets are within the limits for a pensioner concession card, assuming you were otherwise eligible for one (asked for war widows, mothers and MRCA partners only)
      `I receive the VEA extreme disablement rate or special rate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you receive a DVA disability pension at the extreme disablement adjustment rate (s 22(4)) or the special rate (s 24, often called TPI) of the Veterans' Entitlements Act 1986
      `I receive, or have at some time been eligible for, the MRCA Special Rate Disability Pension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you receive the Special Rate Disability Pension under the Military Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2004, or have been eligible for it at any time in your life
      `there is a dwelling on the land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there is a dwelling on the land the rates are levied on: a building, or part of a building, used as a place to live (a house, a unit, a flat)
      `I live in that dwelling as my sole or principal place of living` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that dwelling is your only or main home
      `how many of the others liable are my spouse or de facto partner living with me` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of the other people liable for the rates on this land are your husband, wife or de facto partner whose only or main home is the same as yours (0 or 1; 0 if you are the only person liable)
      `how many of the others liable are other eligible pensioners living with me` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of the other people liable for the rates are themselves eligible pensioners living in this dwelling as their only or main home
      `how many of the others liable are the spouse or de facto partner of another eligible pensioner, living with me` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of the other people liable are the husband, wife or de facto partner of another eligible pensioner (not you), sharing that pensioner's home, which is also your only or main home
      `how many of the others liable are none of these` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of the other people liable for the rates are none of the above: for example a son or daughter who is not an eligible pensioner, a co-owner who lives elsewhere, or your spouse or partner if their main home is elsewhere
      `the part of the rates that I and those living with me are liable for` IS A NUMBER @desc As between all the people liable, the part of the rates that you and the people counted in the first three answers are liable for, as a fraction of the whole (for example 0.5 for half); used only if someone in the last group is liable with you
      `my ordinary rates for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc The ordinary rates levied on the land for the year, in dollars, as on your rates notice (if part is postponed under Division 2, only the part not postponed)
      `my domestic waste management charges for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc The annual charges for domestic waste management services (household rubbish collection) levied on the land for the year, in dollars
      `my water supply special rates or charges for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc The council's water supply special rates or charges levied on the land for the year, in dollars (0 if the council does not supply your water, as in Sydney Water and Hunter Water areas)
      `my sewerage special rates or charges for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc The council's sewerage special rates or charges levied on the land for the year, in dollars (0 if the council does not provide your sewerage)
      `my other rates or charges for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc Any other rate or charge the council levied on the land for the year, in dollars, such as another special rate or a stormwater management charge (0 if none)
      `the rating year` IS A NUMBER @desc The rating year the rates are for, named by the year it starts: 2025 for 1 July 2025 to 30 June 2026
      `the day my rates notice was served` IS A DATE @desc The day the council's rates and charges notice for that year was served on you (rates are levied by serving the notice)
      `the day I became an eligible pensioner` IS A DATE @desc The first day on which you met all the conditions of an eligible pensioner for this dwelling (any earlier day if you met them before the notice was served)
      `a regulation has varied the reduction amounts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a NSW regulation made under s 580 has varied the amounts of the pensioner reduction (the $250 and $87.50 limits); answer no unless you know it has
      `the council has made a hardship order that covers me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the council has made an order under s 577 to avoid hardship that covers you or this dwelling (treating someone as an eligible pensioner, or as solely liable)
      `the council has waived or reduced my rates under s 582` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the council has chosen to waive or reduce your rates, charges or interest under s 582 of the Act, beyond the standard pensioner reduction
GIVETH A `Reduction answer`
DECIDE `How much are my rates and charges reduced this year` IS
    `the s 575 reduction for`
        (`my Commonwealth payments and card from` `I receive a pension, benefit or allowance under Chapter 2 of the Social Security Act` `I receive a service pension under Part III of the Veterans' Entitlements Act` `I am entitled to a pensioner concession card` `I receive a DVA pension as a war widow or war widower` `I receive a DVA pension as the unmarried or widowed mother of a deceased unmarried member of the Defence or Peacekeeping Forces` `I have received the MRCA s 234(1)(b) lump sum or receive the weekly amount` `my income and assets would not stop me being granted a pensioner concession card` `I receive the VEA extreme disablement rate or special rate` `I receive, or have at some time been eligible for, the MRCA Special Rate Disability Pension`)
        (`my occupation from` `there is a dwelling on the land` `I live in that dwelling as my sole or principal place of living`)
        (`my liability from` `how many of the others liable are my spouse or de facto partner living with me` `how many of the others liable are other eligible pensioners living with me` `how many of the others liable are the spouse or de facto partner of another eligible pensioner, living with me` `how many of the others liable are none of these` `the part of the rates that I and those living with me are liable for`)
        (`my rates from` `my ordinary rates for the year` `my domestic waste management charges for the year` `my water supply special rates or charges for the year` `my sewerage special rates or charges for the year` `my other rates or charges for the year`)
        `the rating year`
        `the day my rates notice was served`
        `the day I became an eligible pensioner`
        (`the relief from` `a regulation has varied the reduction amounts` `the council has made a hardship order that covers me` `the council has waived or reduced my rates under s 582`)

§§ `When my concession ends`

-- Asked only if something has happened that ends your entitlement (you stop receiving the payment, lose the card, move
-- out, or sell).
@export Something has changed and I am no longer entitled to the NSW pensioner rates reduction. On what day does my concession end (s 584(1) of the Local Government Act 1993)?
GIVEN `the day my circumstances changed` IS A DATE @desc The day the change happened that ended your entitlement (for example the day your pension stopped, or the day you moved out)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `On what day does my concession end` IS
    `the day the entitlement ceases after a change on` `the day my circumstances changed`

@export My NSW pensioner rates concession has ended. How much of what I paid for the year is credited to the rest of the year (s 584(2) of the Local Government Act 1993)?
GIVEN `the day my circumstances changed` IS A DATE @desc The day the change happened that ended your entitlement (for example the day your pension stopped, or the day you moved out)
      `I had paid the whole year's reduced rates in full` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, by the end of the quarter in which the change happened, you had paid the whole year's rates and charges, as reduced for pensioners, in full
      `what I paid for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount you paid for the whole year's reduced rates and charges, in dollars
GIVETH A `Credit answer`
DECIDE `How much of what I paid is credited when my concession ends` IS
    `the s 584(2) credit after a change on` `the day my circumstances changed` `paid in full` `what I paid for the year`
    WHERE
        `paid in full` MEANS `I had paid the whole year's reduced rates in full`

§§ `Can the council recover what it wrote off?`

@export Can the council take proceedings to recover a pensioner reduction of my NSW rates that it wrote off (s 583(2) of the Local Government Act 1993)?
GIVEN `it was written off because of a wilfully false statement in my application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the reduction was written off because of a statement in your application that you knew to be false
      `it was written off for a period after my entitlement ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the amount was written off for a quarter after your entitlement ended under s 584 (after the last day of the quarter in which your circumstances changed)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the council recover the reduction it wrote off` IF
    `the council may take proceedings to recover the amount written off` `it was written off because of a wilfully false statement in my application` `it was written off for a period after my entitlement ended`

§§ `Other relief the council may choose to give`

-- s 582 relief is at the council's discretion; only whether the council is allowed to give it is answered.
@export Is my NSW council allowed to waive or reduce my rates, charges and interest under s 582 of the Local Government Act 1993 and Regulation cl 136 (a choice for the council, beyond the standard pensioner reduction)?
GIVEN `I receive a pension, benefit or allowance under Chapter 2 of the Social Security Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you receive a Centrelink payment under Chapter 2 of the Social Security Act 1991 (Cth), such as the age pension, disability support pension, carer payment, parenting payment, JobSeeker payment or youth allowance
      `I hold a pensioner concession card` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a Commonwealth pensioner concession card (being entitled to one is not enough here: you must hold it)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the council allowed to waive or reduce my rates under s 582` IF
